; Cost-modeling an in-loop extended reduction (reduce.add(zext/sext(narrow)))
; with a scalable VF used to crash in AArch64TTIImpl::getExtendedReductionCost,
; which queried VecVT.getSizeInBits() >= 64 on a (simple) scalable MVT and thus
; implicitly converted a scalable TypeSize to a fixed-width scalar
; (reportFatalInternalError). The scalable case must instead fall through to the
; generic BasicTTIImpl cost path, which costs the reduction and the extend
; separately, so the extended-reduction expression is not profitable and not
; formed for that VF. These functions must not crash.

